\begin_body

\begin_layout Paragraph*

\series bold
Model definition
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset VSpace bigskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\mathbf{v}_{t}=\mathbf{p}\odot\mathbf{v}_{t-1}+(1-\mathbf{p})\odot(D_{in}SD_{out}g(\mathbf{v}_{t-1})+\mathbf{b}+\mathbf{c}\odot\mathbf{u}_{t})
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $\odot$
\end_inset

 is the Hadamard (element-wise) product.
 You can equivalently turn the lefthand vector into a diagonal matrix.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Vectors are bolded and are 
\begin_inset Formula $n$
\end_inset

 dimensional column vectors.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{v}_{t}$
\end_inset

 is a vector of the neural activity or 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

voltage
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 of each of the ~50k neurons in the model.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{p}$
\end_inset

 is a vector which determines the persistence of a neuron.
 i.e.
 at given time step how much of its current activity is determined by its previous activity vs synaptic input.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $S$
\end_inset

 is a matrix of signed synapse counts from the connectome.
 Sign is determined by that cell's neurotransmitter,
 estimated from the connectome.
 Row 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 lists all the synaptic inputs to neuron 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 and a column 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 lists all outgoing synaptic connections of neuron 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $D_{in}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $D_{out}$
\end_inset

 are diagonal matrices that scale the total input and output of each neuron.
 These scale the rows and columns of 
\begin_inset Formula $S$
\end_inset

 respectively.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $g$
\end_inset

 is a point-wise nonlinearity.
 Currently a softplus 
\begin_inset Formula $g(x)=\log(1+e^{x})$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{b}$
\end_inset


\series default
 is a vector of each neuron's bias.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{c}$
\end_inset

 is a vector which determines the strength of the external stimulus to a neuron.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{u}_{t}$
\end_inset

 is a vector of the stimulus to a neuron at time 
\begin_inset Formula $t$
\end_inset

.
 In the model this is only nonzero for L1,
 L2,
 and L3 which receive visual stimulation.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{p}$
\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Formula $D_{in}$
\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Formula $D_{out}$
\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{b}$
\end_inset

,
 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{c}$
\end_inset

 are learned.
\end_layout

